  recipeId: resistor
  concept: "Authored objective: Correct Resistor Voltage.\nAuthored requirement:
    Measure 2.7-3.3 V across current-limiting resistor R_LIMIT. voltage \u2265 2.7
    V. voltage \u2264 3.3 V. Connection pair R_LIMIT_Input and R_LIMIT_Output. Conduction
    required.\nGeneral teaching principle: Resistance, voltage and current are linked
    by Ohm's law for ideal resistors, while power dissipation needs separate evaluation.\nOnly
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A flow restriction can suggest resistance; unlike a pipe, a resistor follows
    electrical laws.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Current and resistor power cannot be established without voltage/current
    evidence and component values.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Correct Resistor Voltage\u2019, which component,
    reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should you inspect
    first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Correct Resistor Voltage\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 14, perform the objective \u2018Correct Resistor Voltage\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Measure 2.7-3.3
    V across current-limiting resistor R_LIMIT. voltage \u2265 2.7 V. voltage \u2264
    3.3 V. Connection pair R_LIMIT_Input and R_LIMIT_Output. Conduction required.\nThe
    mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
